/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  reactions -- STAGE D ONLY.  Stages A, B and C carry no reactions library:
  A declares a conversion, B and C minimise Gibbs energy.  A rate law is what
  stage D adds, and it is the ONE thing this file declares.

  THE RATE LAW IS NOT WRITTEN HERE.  `type dysonSimon1968;` selects the
  correlation object curated in
  src/unitOperations/reactor/kinetics/AmmoniaSynthesisRate.{H,cpp}:

      D. C. Dyson and J. M. Simon, "A kinetic expression with diffusion
      correction for ammonia synthesis on industrial catalyst", Ind. Eng.
      Chem. Fundam. 7 (1968) 605-610 -- Eqs 2, 6-8, 18, 19, 39 + Table I, 40.

  Every constant (the Arrhenius pair of Eq 18/19, Gillespie & Beattie's Ka of
  Eq 2, the fugacity-coefficient correlations of Eqs 6-8, the 21 constants of
  Table I) is the paper's own and lives in that one file with its citation,
  its validity window and five verification anchors; the engine prints the
  citation and the window on every run.  A case may not re-type them, and
  this block REFUSES a key the law does not read -- an `A`, an `Ea`, an
  `order`, a `reversible` -- because a number the engine does not read is a
  comment that looks like a declaration.  Read the props bench first:
  tutorials/props/kinetics/ammoniaRate01_dyson_simon.

  WHAT IS DECLARED, and why each is a declaration and not a default:

    roles {}             WHICH of this case's components play the law's N2,
                         H2 and NH3.  The engine will not infer them from
                         names; everything else (argon here) is inert to
                         Eq 19.

    effectivenessFactor  `intrinsic` = Equation 19 alone: the effectiveness
                         factor is taken as 1, and the engine says on every
                         run that this is UNPRICED -- the paper's own
                         diffusion correction (Eq 39 with Table I, for 6-10 mm
                         particles at 150-300 atm) exists in the engine and is
                         NOT applied here.  That is deliberate and it is stage
                         D's stated limit: the pellet is the rung beyond D
                         (DEV.md C8).  `dysonSimonEq39` prices it and needs
                         `operation { catalyst { particleDiameter ...; } }` on
                         the reactor; the README measures what it changes.

  UNITS.  Equation 19 returns kg-mol of NH3 per cubic metre of catalyst BED
  per hour, so the reactor's `V_R` IS the catalyst volume and there is no
  `catalystLoading` (the engine refuses one under this law).  The pressure
  the law needs, in atmospheres, is read off the inlet stream and converted
  at the reactor; nothing here is typed in the paper's units.

  THE STOICHIOMETRY is checked against the law: it must be N2 + 3 H2 -> 2 NH3
  up to a positive factor, with no other component carrying a nu, because
  the law is that reaction's rate and no other's.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

ammoniaSynthesis
{
    stoichiometry
    (
        { component N2;   nu -1; }
        { component H2;   nu -3; }
        { component NH3;  nu  2; }
    );

    kinetics
    {
        type                 dysonSimon1968;
        roles { N2 N2;  H2 H2;  NH3 NH3; }
        effectivenessFactor  intrinsic;       // Eq 19; xi = 1 UNPRICED (announced)
    }
}
